In `faker.providers.misc.Provider.password`, each enabled category appends one entry to `required_tokens`. With `special_chars=True`, `digits=True`, `upper_case=True`, and `lower_case=True`, the loop condition is trying to grow `random_indexes` until it contains 4 unique indices. The loop body adds one `randint(0, len(chars) - 1)` result to a set each time, so repeated draws can leave the set size unchanged. For the test's seeded call sequence, the first several draws include repeats, and the fourth distinct index is reached on the 8th execution of that `add(...)` line.

## Answer
{"loop_iteration_count":8}
